-- title:
--   A k₀-form F₀ of the full-level field, q=2
-- statement:
--   Let $q$ be a prime with $q = 2$, let $M' \neq 0$ with $q \nmid M'$, and let $A$ be a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ for which $q$ is a non-unit of $A$; write $\kappa$ for the residue field of $A$. Let $W$ be a finite set of places of `modularFunctionFieldC κ M'` over $\kappa$ whose members are exactly the supersingular places `ssPlaces q M' κ` (rational affine geometric places whose value at the geometric $j$-generator lies in the supersingular $j$-set). Assume the base-changed full-level-$M'$ field `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` is contained in $F =$ `fieldBar q M'`, the base change to $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ of the $X_H$-field of level $q^2M'$ with $H =$ `levelH q M'`, and let $R_0$ be a constant reduction of $A$ from `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` to `modularFunctionFieldC κ M'` which, on elements represented by Laurent series with coefficients in $A$, is given by coefficientwise reduction. Fix a primitive $q$-th root of unity $\zeta$ in $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, a family $O^{\mathrm{Ig}}$ of valuation subrings of $F$ indexed by the projective line over $\mathbb{Z}/q$ and a family $O^{\mathrm{SS}}$ indexed by $W$, subject to the hypotheses summarised here: $O^{\mathrm{Ig}}$ at the point $\infty$ consists of the quotients $x/y$ of Laurent series with coefficients in $A$ whose denominator has nonzero reduction; the remaining $O^{\mathrm{Ig}}(\ell)$ are the pullbacks of $O^{\mathrm{Ig}}(\infty)$ along the level automorphisms `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ` for $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ moving $\infty$ to $\ell$, the family is injective, and the level automorphisms permute it; each $O^{\mathrm{SS}}(s)$ meets $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ in exactly $A$, is fixed by every `levelAutBar q M' ζ' γ` with $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$, contains a element $t$ with $t - a$ a unit for every $a \in A$, and reduces compatibly with $R_0$ and $s$ on those $f \in R_0$.`integers` which are regular wherever the $q$-expansion of $j$ is. Assume further that $O^{\mathrm{Ig}}(\infty)$ is the integer ring of a regular prolongation $R$ of $A$ with values in `xHFunctionFieldC κ (q^2*M') (levelH q M')`, that $R_0$.`integers` is the preimage of $O^{\mathrm{Ig}}(\infty)$, that $A$ contains a $(q^2-1)$-st root of $q$, and the small-constant hypotheses: an intermediate field $k_0$ of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}/\mathbb{Q}$ such that $A \cap k_0$ is a henselian discrete valuation ring with algebraically closed residue field, uniformised by an element $\pi_0$ of $k_0$, with every element of $A$ congruent modulo the maximal ideal to an element of $k_0 \cap A$; finally a prime $\ell \geq 3$ with $\ell \neq q$ and $\ell \nmid M'$, an element $\zeta_0$ of $k_0$ that is a primitive $q\ell$-th root of unity, and an element $\varpi_t$ of $k_0 \cap A$ with $\varpi_t^{q^2-1} = q u$ for some unit $u$ of $A$. Then, $F$ being a $k_0$-algebra through $k_0 \hookrightarrow \overline{\mathbb{Q}} \hookrightarrow F$, there is an intermediate field $F_0$ of $F/k_0$ such that: the compositum of $F_0$ with the $k_0$-subfield generated by the image of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ is all of $F$; $F_0$ is stable under `levelAutBar q M' ζ' γ` for every primitive $q$-th root of unity $\zeta'$ and every $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$; for every intermediate field $K'$ of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}/k_0$ finite over $k_0$, every finite family $(c_i)$ in $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ linearly independent over $K'$ and every family $(a_i)$ in the compositum of $F_0$ with the $k_0$-subfield generated by the image of $K'$, the relation $\sum_i c_i a_i = 0$ forces $a_i = 0$ for all $i$; and every $f \in F$ whose Laurent series has rational coefficients, i.e. lies in the image of `coeffEmb`, belongs to $F_0$.
--
--   This provides a form over the small field $k_0$ of the full-level function field $F = \overline{\mathbb{Q}}\cdot F(\Gamma_H(q^2M'))$: a level-stable intermediate field which is regular over $k_0$ (linearly disjoint from $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ over every finite subextension) and which absorbs all functions with rational $q$-expansion, in particular $j$ and its level-$M'$ companion. It is the $q = 2$ case, whose binders differ from the case $5 \le q$ only in the hypothesis $q = 2$, and it feeds the construction of the Igusa base model with smooth point stalks in [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_igusaBaseModel_smoothPointStalks_of_eq_two`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_igusaBaseModel_smoothPointStalks_of_eq_two).
